<%- include('partials/header',{narrow:true}) %>
<div class="page-heading">
<div>
<div class="eyebrow">ADMINISTRATOR</div>
<h1>Environment setup</h1>
<p>A simple checklist for getting your workspace ready.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section aria-labelledby="required-settings">
<h2 id="required-settings">What you need to connect your tools</h2>
<p class="helper">Configure these on the server with <code>npm run setup</code>. Secrets are loaded from AWS Secrets Manager (Floci locally). Credential values are never displayed here. “Configured” means present, not that a real grant has been tested.</p>
<% for(const group of requirements) { %>
<article class="panel requirement-group">
<h3><%= group.name %></h3>
<% for(const field of group.fields) { %>
<div class="requirement-field">
<div><strong><%= field.name %></strong><p><%= field.help %></p><code><%= field.location %></code></div>
<span class="badge <%= field.configured?'active':'pending' %>"><%= field.status %></span>
</div>
<% } %>
</article>
<% } %>
<div class="note"><strong>Ready to configure?</strong> Run <code>npm run setup</code>, follow the prompts. Then run <code>npm run doctor -- --online</code>. Never paste private keys into access requests or send them to users.</div>
</section>
<h2 class="section-heading history-heading">Runtime checks</h2>
<div class="panel checklist">
<% for(const check of checks) { %>
<div>
<span class="check-icon <%= check.ok?'ok':'attention' %>">
<%= check.ok?'✓':'!' %>
</span>
<div>
<h3>
<%= check.name %>
</h3>
<p>
<%= check.description %>
</p>
</div>
</div>
<% } %>
</div>
<h2 class="section-heading history-heading">Delivery & provider issues</h2>
<p class="helper">
<%= pendingMail %> email(s) waiting to send · <%= failedMail %> failed delivery attempt(s).
</p>
<% if(!issues.length && !failedMail) { %>
<div class="panel compact-empty">
<strong>No recorded failures.</strong>
<p>Live provider connectivity must still be tested with a dedicated resource.</p>
</div>
<% } %>
<% for(const issue of issues) { %>
<div class="alert warning">
<a href="/requests/<%= issue.id %>">
<strong>Request #<%= issue.id %>
</strong>
</a> · <%= issue.error %>
</div>
<% } %>
<details class="panel operator-details">
<summary>How do I add resources or users?</summary>
<p>Update <code>config/catalog.json</code> to add repositories, accounts, and allowed permissions. Update <code>config/identities.json</code> to enroll users using their OIDC subject. Restart the web and worker services after changes.</p>
<p>Requests keep a snapshot of their resource and identity mapping so existing grants can still expire. Keep the Secrets Manager bundle, GitHub App and AWS workload permissions until those grants are removed.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/guide#operators">Environment setup walkthrough →</a>
</details>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
